. /****************************************************************************
> ***
>  C2_A1_07_sweep2.do -- rerun C2: SWEEP2 sensitivities (A1.5 rows)
>  Usage (cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  stata-mp -b -q do C2_A1_07_sweep2.do <vi
> ntage>
>  Output: ${OUT}/results/A1_parts/A1_07.csv (rows item A1.5, specs below; A1_c
> ombine.py picks it up),
>          ${OUT}/tables/A1_A1.5_sw2_exclusion_counts.csv, log, nflow records i
> n A1_nflow.csv.
>  Definitions (authors' working notes; cell rule = SW2_09_classify.py:17-28:
>  a row is flagged if its reverse cell (reporter iso3_o, basis_rev_*) or its s
> ame-direction cell
>  (reporter iso3_d, basis_same_*) is a flagged reporter-year-series):
>    visitors: MDA nationality 2007-2015; KAZ residence 2020-2021; SAU residenc
> e, ZAF residence,
>              BOL nationality, NOR residence 2020-2021 (tourists-only visitor 
> values)
>    tourists: BLR nationality 2007-2020 (organised tourism only); KAZ residenc
> e 2020-2021
>    trade:    six unexplained single lots PAN->RUS 2013, NZL->SGP 2017, RUS->H
> KG 2019, RUS->EGY 2018,
>              KOR->VEN 2012, CAN->GTM 2021, and NOR->SAU 2019 (record absent f
> rom current Comtrade);
>              exporter -> importer = iso3_o -> iso3_d
>  Specs: x_sw2defn (definitional mobility flags, joint), x_clean_sw2 (A1.5 (vi
> ) "clean measurement"
>  x_clean of A1_02_measurement.do lines 351-381, recomputed here verbatim, plu
> s x_sw2defn), x_sw2lots.
>  Positive controls: (1) the x_clean fit reproduces A1_02's row A1.5.x_clean.<
> m>.mob_bilat_<m> of the
>  same vintage (|db| < 1e-9, same N); (2) corrected vintage: flagged baseline 
> rows per finding =
>  05_output/11_data_screens/NEW_FINDINGS_COUNTS.csv (507, 90 / 318, 146, 136, 
> 242, 84, 80; lots 6 / 0).
>  Help consulted: ppmlhdfe.sthlp 2.3.4 (absorb(), vce(cluster), e(N_full), e(n
> um_singletons),
>  e(num_separated), e(converged)); [D] merge; [D] import delimited; nflow.sthl
> p 1.0.1.
>  No data value is altered: every restriction is an if-condition.
> *****************************************************************************
> **/
. args vintage

. clear all

. set more off

. set varabbrev off

. set linesize 200

. version 18.0

. do "00_config.do" `vintage'

. /*******************************************************************************
>  00_config.do  --  globals for one data vintage (analysis layer of the replication package)
> 
>  Usage (from another do-file, cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  do 00_config.do <vintage>
>    <vintage> = corrected2x (revised baseline, default run)
>              | corrected | corrected2 (reconciliation switch, same data build)
>              | submitted (reconciliation switch, needs a second build with corrections off)
>  Every path is built from the package root ${PKGROOT}, which run_all.py passes as the first
>  argument of the generated wrapper do-file (_run.do pattern); nothing here is machine-specific.
>  Defines globals only and checks the Stata version.
> 
>  Vintages (see README.md, "Data-correction rules"):
>    corrected   = build with the correction rules on (code 490 -> TWN, Paraguay residence quarantine, flags)
>    corrected2  = corrected + quarantine of PAK residence 2020-2021 and BLR visitors-by-residence
>                  partner LIE 2020-2022 (same rule as Paraguay); 31-code outcome
>    corrected2x = corrected2 with the 30-code outcome (31-code basket minus HS 490700) = revised baseline
>    submitted   = original data as submitted (build with corrections off), for the reconciliation only
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
. args vintage

. if !inlist("`vintage'", "submitted", "corrected", "corrected2", "corrected2x") {
